All in good time. In my early games I level up the pet. It becomes the
enforcer early on. Levelling up yourself is always an arms race. You
get benefits (Better HP and PP) but at the cost of tougher monsters.

Also there are several tricks to get the benefits without the downside.
Two examples are letting a newt knock you under 5HP and then praying.
Your god will typically add 3-5 HP to your max HP just for the asking.
Of course blessed healing potions will up your Max HP also. You can eat
newts to get a PP bump.

Finally there's usually enough money flowing that you can affort to level 
up to level 2 or 3 without too much harm. But if you can pull off getting
protection at level 1, it only takes 2 shops worth of money fo accomplish.

AC and speed are critical early game survival indicators. So protection
which gives you a ton of AC with no weight is better than gold.

